Shell Script--> A Plain text file contaiting a sequential list of shell commands executed as an automated problem.

Shebug/Hashbang-->
#!/bin/bash  --> Fist line of the code (In starting of every single shell Script)

Create a Shell Script-->
-touch script.sh    [script.sh (File Name)]
 sh --> is the extention of the shell script

-vi script.sh   [vi --> use for open the file]

Comments--> Similar to python uses '#' for commenting

Printing --> Uses echo function similar to python
Example:  echo "Hello World"

Running a Shell Program -->
-chmod +x script.sh   
[chmod means change mode for the file]
[+x means creating an executable file]

-./script.sh  [current directory]

Variables --> Dynamic Variables similar to python
Example: 
username="ABC"
age = 25
Note: There is no spacing between the '=' sign var naming similar to c/c++

To Print Variables need to use '$' sign infront of varname
Example: echo $username

To directly concate two strings use curly braces {}
Example: echo "$ {username} s"
         echo "$ {age}+2"
        
To treat Variables as int use two pair of first brackets with spaces in between them
Example: echo " $ ((age+2))"

Directly using OS Variables
Example: $ (pwd)
Use a pair of brackets along with the var name in between


